      "heading": null,
      "bodyHtml": "<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For the geolocation of construction site tools, different technologies can be used. The choice of one technology over another will depend on various criteria, such as the type of infrastructure desired, the number and size of the equipment to be geolocated, the environment in which the solution will be installed, the cost of the infrastructure and finally, the level of precision required. To geolocate construction site tools, Jaxicloud Innovation offers location beacons based on 3 different technologies: Bluetooth Low Energy, Wirepas Mesh and Quuppa AOA.</span></p><p>The equipment to be Geo-located will be equipped with BLE beacons that periodically emit an identification number. These numbers will be picked up by nearby BLE receivers (e.g. smartphones, PCs, GPS boxes or even gateways). The information will then be transmitted to client servers via the cloud or via Ethernet networks . The end user will be able to consult the data in real time on a business platform and set up alerts if necessary.</p><p>The end user will be able to consult the data in real time on a business platform and set up alerts if necessary.</p>",
      "bodyText": "For the geolocation of construction site tools, different technologies can be used. The choice of one technology over another will depend on various criteria, such as the type of infrastructure desired, the number and size of the equipment to be geolocated, the environment in which the solution will be installed, the cost of the infrastructure and finally, the level of precision required. To geolocate construction site tools, Jaxicloud Innovation offers location beacons based on 3 different technologies: Bluetooth Low Energy, Wirepas Mesh and Quuppa AOA.The equipment to be Geo-located will be equipped with BLE beacons that periodically emit an identification number. These numbers will be picked up by nearby BLE receivers (e.g. smartphones, PCs, GPS boxes or even gateways). The information will then be transmitted to client servers via the cloud or via Ethernet networks . The end user will be able to consult the data in real time on a business platform and set up alerts if necessary.The end user will be able to consult the data in real time on a business platform and set up alerts if necessary.",
